WEBVTT

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.800
I'm on my way!

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.700
Woot, Horizon!

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.160
Bind, Slicing Dragonfly.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.540
See you next week!

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.590
Keep working!

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.640
With our food supplies in,

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.530
I'm guessing we'll be partying big time tonight.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.900
Wasn't our teacher aboard the diplomatic ship?

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.360
In which case...

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.660
We'll have grilled meat...

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.530
Mito! Masazumi! How have you been?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.050
Asama!

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:20.790
The Chancellor!

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.040
The Chancellor rose from the ocean!

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:33.470
Come and greet the morning, Horizon!

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.950
What is it? You're being loud.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:43.520
I call it my "rampantly growing, mineral rich seaweed armor".

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:50.110
Horizon, you've always been able to strip away the armor of my heart.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.100
What's going on?!

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.740
What would you do if you caught a cold while you were running about naked?

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:02.910
What are you doing?

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.420
I am terribly sorry.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.380
I was refining some essentials in rest-mode,

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.300
so I am going back to sleep.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.760
Good night, everyone.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.760
Good night...

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.840
Suzu, I'm amazed this doesn't bug you.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.460
I-It's the same... as a gangway.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.060
It's just warped.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.190
What's wrong?

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.610
S-Some noise has been going, "Gong! Gong!"

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:35.240
England's Level 1 area is off in that direction.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.770
London Tower should be just before it.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.390
Uh, um...

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:57.360
Why?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.580
Oh, well, you see!

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.350
There is something wrong with the cemetery grounds over there,

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.170
so I was on my way to inform the locals.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.270
Why did you stop me back there?

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.900
One such as yourself should have been able to identify the spell I was about to use.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.410
I totally didn't catch on to what you were doing.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.120
Why are you putting yourself in a losing position?

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.600
Anyway, I failed to pay close enough attention.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.360
Hey, there, Tenzo!

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:31.880
Why don't you tidy up the graveyard with that good sir?

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.230
Didn't you say,

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.430
"That graveyard needeth to be either repairedth or movedth"?

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:39.510
You're saying that all wrong!

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.130
That's noble speech!

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:45.350
Is that... the Far East spirit, Wet Man?!

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.200
Huh?

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.020
Hey, there! Dude in the cloak!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.700
You've got some naming sense there!

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.100
You're no pushover, are you?

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.430
R-Right...

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.890
What are you talking about?

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.690
So what are you going to do now?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.390
I intend to confirm the state of the cemetery,

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:06.040
decide if it needs to be repaired or relocated and then do as needed.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.300
That simplifies matters!

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.500
Tenzo, give the guy a hand.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.620
Wait, but I shouldn't...

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.590
Judge!

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.300
Eh?! But, I—

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.330
Hey! Wait a second!

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.570
Master Muneshige,

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.980
what should I do now?

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.220
Even when unconscious,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.800
Master Muneshige sets my heart racing.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.670
D-Don't do anything rash, Tachibana!

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:16.900
Chancellor...?

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.490
Oh, huh?

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:26.290
So, may I clean the room?

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.790
If that is all, then I shall do it.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:33.290
Or is it inappropriate for me to be with Master Muneshige?

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:38.750
No, I think there is nothing wrong with someone wanting to be with somebody.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.880
Then the one who revoked Master Muneshige's title was...

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.350
Tes. It was Juana.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:51.230
I imagine she was thinking how Hashiba may still pay a fortune for the title "Peerless Man of the West".

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.790
Didn't you discuss this with Lady Juana?

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.940
She can handle things without being specifically asked.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.280
But...

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.030
I feel uncomfortable ordering people around.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.310
If you were to die,

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:07.260
would you continue to stay with him?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.540
Well... Tes.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.350
I think that's for the best.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:15.760
Chancellor, didn't your family stay with you?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.430
It's hard to say...

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.050
Well, I'll let you clean up in here.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:19.920
Chancellor!

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:24.420
If I did something great for our nation,

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.700
may I request that you return Master Muneshige's title?

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:31.080
You two would have to join the Hashibas.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:31.980
Are you okay with that?

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.180
Tes.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.190
As long as I can be with Master Muneshige...

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:39.030
After all, Master Muneshige was the one

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:43.000
who severed my arms and gave me a normal life in their place.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.300
Please bring the swords here.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.870
Please use this cloth to wipe the swords placed here once.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.790
Please take the wiped down swords to the ones lined up over there.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.030
Most impressive!

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:04.630
Kobolds can only accept simple orders,

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:08.390
but they can handle impressive tasks when you delegate the work.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:09.460
I see...

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.440
I'm impressed you could pull it out so easily.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.270
I've got a wee little trick.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:20.350
First you push it straight down.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:26.330
That makes the blade cut into the earth, thus widening the hole.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:27.310
All that's left...

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.980
And there you have it.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:36.120
You may be able to draw Excalibur Caliburn.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.680
I doubt that.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.700
Even Queen Mary or whoever couldn't draw it, remember?

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:44.840
That is because Double Bloody Mary was a failure of a woman.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:47.510
So she wasn't worthy of becoming king?

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:48.760
Judge.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.070
She was Mary Tudor and Mary Stuart.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.800
There was a time when people thought she might,

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.690
seeing as she had succeeded the name of two queens.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:01.360
But at present, she is locked away in London Tower.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:06.070
To top it off, her execution is what will bring in the Spanish Armada,

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:10.520
so the name "Mary" is nothing but a curse to England.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.280
It must be tough...

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.270
Why?!

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:16.460
It is essential for England that she spend her life like this!

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.640
And you call that "tough"?

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.270
I lack the words to describe

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:24.510
willingly accepting such losses as anything but "tough."

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:29.860
Then why do you think she follows through with this foolishness?

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:34.180
Probably because someone else will suffer the loss if she doesn't.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:41.130
But even so, there must be times when she feels anguish or gets wounded.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:45.830
I hope that someone is there for her during such times of hardship.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.950
C-Crap! I spoke out of line!

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.030
Reflect on what you said.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:54.540
What's wrong?

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.160
It-It's nothing...

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:09.010
A busty blond?!

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.010
Th-Thank you... very much.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.960
Master... Scarred?

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:15.830
Judge.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.060
Huh?

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:20.340
Sorry, but do you see a book anywhere?

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.230
A book?

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.350
A Dictionary of Far Eastern Slang?

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:28.740
Thank goodness!

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:32.490
Milton said, "They'll make light of you if they discover you're a woman."

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.490
You're dead if you make light of her.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.940
Talk about tough.

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:40.610
I'm sure speaking with me must have been difficult.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.620
I, Tenzo, appreciate your efforts.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.870
S-Sorry!

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.960
Did I say something that hurt your feelings?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:54.010
No, I should be the one apologizing to you.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:57.970
Could you please avoid telling anyone that I am a woman?

00:10:58.270 --> 00:10:59.970
Judge. You got it.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.630
What a relief!

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:06.980
And, may I call you Master Tenzo?

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.480
I'm a "Master" now!

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.360
Hey, Tenzo! Could I ask ya for a favor?

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.950
Wh-What on Earth is it?

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:19.210
Sis is starting to say ingenious things like, "I want a bath!"

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.040
So, are there any warm springs around?

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:24.040
Warm springs, huh?

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.760
What did he say, Foolish Brother?

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:31.700
Yeah, he said he'd make some!

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:32.880
Who's there?!

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:38.560
Hey, sorry about that, people.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.230
If I said I had no intention of alarming you,

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.150
would you believe me?

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.820
Trump 9, Ben Jonson!

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:52.040
I am honored that you remembered, Lady.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.520
This is Trump 2, F. Walsingham.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.860
She is here as my bodyguard.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:04.460
And this is Trump 7, Charles Howard.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:07.750
He owns a British fleet and serves as our treasurer.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:32.660
Wow!

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:33.940
H-He prostrated?!

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:34.700
Snap, snap!

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:34.860
<b>Snap Shot</b>

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:35.200
Snap, snap!

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:35.360
<b>Snap Shot</b>

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.640
I'm begging you!

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:42.080
Could you please save England?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.990
<i>Wh-What a perfect prostration!</i>

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:52.830
It's noisy.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:00.740
What's this...?

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.060
It's a Musashi specialty: fresh sashimi with curry sauce.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:09.160
I'm an athlete, so I am on a special diet.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.510
Go on and help yourselves.

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:15.480
We'll have some later, so don't hold back on our account.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:32.770
<i>The item up for negotiations this time is food.</i>

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:33.960
<i>Meat, to be exact!</i>

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:38.420
<i>Right now, Musashi has 2,000 tons of meat brought in from Mikawa.</i>

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.750
<i>2,000 tons?!</i>

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:44.180
<i>Yep! That's exactly how much meat England burns through in one month.</i>

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.040
Good point. The expiration date is...

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:52.660
Judge. Even with the spells and refrigerated storage,

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:55.100
it will probably only last another two weeks or so.

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:59.330
Meat is delicious right before it spoils, so I love it!

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:01.820
Regardless of how it tastes,

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:04.860
we won't get much money off meat that is about to expire.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.760
Now then, how will he handle these negotiations...?

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.830
Okay, about this transaction...

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.410
Tes. What is it?

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:13.900
Let's not do it.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.750
If you conduct commerce with Musashi,

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:22.590
people will think England has defied the Testament Union.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.340
We do not wish that for you.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.050
Tes.

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:31.980
But, our battle with Tres España is soon at hand.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:34.310
Judge. You mean the Spanish Armada, don't you?

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:37.310
May I inquire as to when the battle will begin?

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.440
That is classified information, so I cannot say.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:45.860
However, our concern is whether or not we will fully consume Musashi's exports before then.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.430
<i>Musashi's meat is good for another two weeks.</i>

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.830
<i>If he isn't sure if they can consume it all before the battle, then...</i>

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.960
<i>"England intends to commence battle with the Spanish Armada within two weeks."</i>

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.190
<i>Considering England's processing capabilities,</i>

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:05.510
<i>if they dedicated the country to working night and day at full capacity,</i>

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:07.340
<i>they could process it within one week.</i>

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:08.920
<i>In which case England will</i>

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.300
<i>draw out the negotiations for another week</i>

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:15.630
<i>before they begin purchasing our meat that will go bad in two.</i>

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:20.120
Musashi would like to save England from its plight.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:24.020
So it is imperative that you not attract the Testament Union's attention.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.530
Is there a way to pull that off?

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:27.610
There is.

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:28.490
And it is?

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:33.320
Musashi and England will hold a joint Spring School Festival.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:36.210
If we hold a festival,

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:39.490
the Musashi Student Council booth could expand beyond meat

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:43.080
and sell various other items as well.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.550
Tes. In that case...

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:47.010
Let's determine the length of the festival.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:54.680
<i>In which case, the amount of time needed to consume a month's worth of meat is...</i>

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:56.640
Two weeks.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.390
Um...

00:15:58.390 --> 00:15:59.640
I don't really follow!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.320
Three days.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.240
<i>He's simply trying to cut the number of days</i>

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.310
<i>to gain the upper hand without regard to</i>

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.080
<i>how long it will take to process the meat.</i>

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.700
<i>Considering the rate of returns,</i>

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:19.440
<i>11 days is the shortest we can cut it.</i>

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:21.080
<i>That's the best we can offer.</i>

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:23.500
One week and seven days for preparations.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.590
Three days and one day for preparations.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.360
One week and five days.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:28.590
Three days and two.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:32.080
We shall handle transporting everything to Scotland.

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.590
In which case we will have a little more money to spend on the festival.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.560
Festivities for three days and preparations for three days.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.310
Seven days and two.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.310
How would a total of nine days sound?

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.430
<i>He just cut off three days?</i>

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.400
<i>If he has to cross the break-even line,</i>

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:47.150
<i>he intends to earn it back through the supplemental income with the festival.</i>

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:50.070
<i>How will their guy respond to our compromise?</i>

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:54.780
To make things easier on you, we shall expand the areas with which you may visit.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.960
We will allow you to visit up to Level 2.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:01.100
In addition, we shall give you an extra day.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.430
Three days of festivities and four days of preparations.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:04.970
That brings it up to seven days,

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:08.500
but, we'd be willing to throw in one more day.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:10.420
Eight days.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:13.430
I hope you find that number acceptable.

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:17.180
Considering the situation, aren't we in a pinch?

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.520
Why?

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:21.300
They have suddenly closed negotiations.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.680
Who do you think we've got over there?

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.650
Master Shirojiro Bertoni.

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:29.530
Yup! And he's Musashi's treasurer.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:31.440
Hold it.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:50.750
Th-That's—

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.760
Do you know what he's doing, Master Tori?

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:55.060
He hasn't done this since he won the Inter-Middle Championship!

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:10.990
It's the Triple Axel Prostration!

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:13.890
That isn't enough time,

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.820
so please reconsider!

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.280
<i>A-A Triple Axel Prostration?!</i>

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:20.770
<i>He didn't even ruffle the long sleeves or pant cuffs</i>

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:23.010
<i>characteristic of Far Eastern uniforms!</i>

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:25.040
<i>He landed without making a sound!</i>

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:27.810
<i>And he's even proffering a box of confectionery!</i>

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:30.120
<i>Is this a prostration to end all prostrations?!</i>

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:30.750
<i>It's magnificent!</i>

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:34.590
<i>I must acknowledge his bow!</i>

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.280
Nine days!

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:39.550
How about three days of festivities and six to prepare?

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.620
Prostrations are amazing, aren't they, Ma'am?

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.430
Amateurs shouldn't try to copy that.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:48.480
Besides, I've made sure to teach everyone...

00:18:49.030 --> 00:18:51.150
...to never do a half-assed job!

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:52.150
Judge.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:56.080
I appreciate your flexibility.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:59.160
Then we'll settle on nine days.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:01.990
No, your negotiation skills were amazing.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.250
You utterly defeated me.

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:05.830
As such, we'd like to relinquish even more days.

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:07.410
No thanks!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.670
Regarding the period of commerce...

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:13.670
Let's lump everything together in three days, as you had initially offered.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:14.860
Three days?!

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:21.700
<i>We're taking advantage of his bluff?</i>

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:24.540
<i>England couldn't process all of that meat in three days.</i>

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.540
<i>They've already negotiated transportation and country entry levels.</i>

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.900
<i>I can't believe this merchant duo!</i>

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:33.780
Tes. I would love to accept your generous offer,

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:39.490
but we do not wish to put you under any additional strain.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:43.030
As such, how about five days of festivities and four of preparations?

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.030
Three days for the festival and two for preparations.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:49.540
Even if you could afford more, I believe this should be enough.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:51.840
Ten days!

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:54.520
Six for the festival and four for preparations.

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:57.010
Wouldn't this allow you to work without feeling encumbered?

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:59.150
You didn't take days off into account, did you?

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.090
Six days for the festival,

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:04.460
one day off and four days for preparations.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.520
What do you say to a total of 11 days?

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:09.440
Te—

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:10.190
One thing more!

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:12.870
Mukai, are you listening?

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:14.990
Wait, Bertoni!

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:17.310
It isn't your place to make this call.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:17.690
Judge.

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:19.780
Then it's in your hands, Vice-President.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:20.590
Judge.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:26.790
Mukai, I'm dispatching you to London as our temporary diplomatic ambassador.

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:29.400
You will be free to contact us.

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.550
Adele, you're going as her bodyguard.

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:33.390
Eh? Okay.

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:34.210
Judge.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:37.100
Wh-Why me...?

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:38.070
Well...

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.040
Isn't it obvious?

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:40.880
H-How so?

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:42.500
Because out of all of us,

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:45.360
you're the one who most clearly speaks her mind and has a stubborn streak,

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:49.350
yet nevertheless takes good care of herself, Bell.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.060
Th-That's not true...

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.030
Don't you worry!

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:56.900
I'm sure that boobless hack of a comedian will work something—

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:01.900
Seijun, your aim is getting better, isn't it?

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.350
Don't do that, M-Masazumi!

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:08.290
Slap-stick comedy is Horizon's department.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.540
<i>She's able to immediately put someone in their place.</i>

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.150
<i>That's why they chose her.</i>

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:15.060
Bell, that's the spirit!

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:18.460
Keep that attitude up while you're our diplomat for a bit!

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:24.890
<i>Right. We think it's coming from London Tower.</i>

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:31.300
Do you think I can handle it...?

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:32.680
It'll be a snap!

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.850
Bell, if you think something seems even a little off,

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.110
feel free to say, "No!"

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.180
A-Am I good enough?

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:43.440
For me to be asking you, it means I think that you're just right.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.160
Then I'll do it!

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:46.620
<b>INARI</b>

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:49.250
Aoi, should we send Futayo as Mukai's bodyguard?
<b>INARI</b>

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:50.610
<b>INARI</b>

00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:51.870
You want to send me?
<b>INARI</b>

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:55.200
Judge. She is Musashi's diplomat.

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:56.290
Know what that means?

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:58.070
She is a representative of the Far East.

00:21:58.590 --> 00:22:01.950
That means she is going in Princess Horizon's place.

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:03.670
Judge. I accept the task.

00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:07.130
You couldn't ask for better hostages, could you?

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:11.740
After all, we're tearing away Musashi's strongest offense and defense.

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:15.350
As a merchant, wouldn't you say this is a marvelous outcome?

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:16.020
Tes.

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:19.300
Seven days for the festival, one day of rest.

00:22:19.300 --> 00:22:21.480
As for preparations, let's see...

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:24.360
After all this, let's give you five days,

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:25.800
bringing it to a total of 13 days.

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:26.580
Judge.

00:22:31.900 --> 00:22:34.130
So then, we'll spend two days on making arrangements.

00:22:34.130 --> 00:22:36.380
After which, we shall enter the School Festival period.

00:22:37.310 --> 00:22:39.750
Tes. May you have lucrative business and good sales!

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:42.930
Judge. May you have lucrative business and good sales!
